      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T16:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I had to re-read through the docs again myself. If you\u0027re building for the default toolchain then things work as written in the gn files (in fact, the default toolchain\u0027s `toolchain_args` isn\u0027t evaluated, which can lead to interesting differences between using a toolchain explicitly and using it as the default). When building for a non-default toolchain the `toolchain_args` is used to override various things (usually just the built-in `current_cpu` and `current_os` like here).\n\nFrom gn\u0027s perspective, \"host\" is where gn runs, \"target\" is what the default toolchain builds for, and \"current\" is what the current toolchain builds for.",
